{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.m_p_m_e_empirical_record","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.m_p_m_e_empirical_record","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L130-L137","doc":"Empirical record: m_p/m_e under compact q-dilog Φ_q vs symmetric\nLi_2^q. The 99.82% gap (vs 1.84% with Faddeev) reflects the\nbar-symmetric projection killing the singular-braid mass scale.\n\nWitness: `m-p-m-e-li2q.witness.json`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization_qEqOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization_qEqOne","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L106-L128","doc":"**Model with the predicate read as its own witness.**  `bar_holds_at`\nis *defined* to be `fun q _n => q = 1`, so the conjectural field\n`bar_holds_at_classical : ∀ n, bar_holds_at 1 n` unfolds to `1 = 1`\nand closes by `rfl`, uniformly in `n`.  Nothing about bar\nsymmetrisation, the Faddeev coefficients or `li2qCoeff` is encoded;\nthe field is satisfied by choosing the predicate to be the equation\nthe field asserts.\n\nThe classical-limit fact it gestures at *is* proved in this file,\nunconditionally and without the class:\n`li2qCoeff_bar_invariant_at_q_eq_one`.  This model does not use it,\nand a real model would.\n\n**A `def`, not an `instance`, since 2026-08-24**, and given a name:\nit was anonymous, so resolution supplied it under the generated name\n`instLi2qPhiqBarSymmetrization`.  Nothing in the corpus takes\n`[Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization]`, so the class documented as consumed\n\"via [Instance] per AGENTS.md §3b-cond\" has no consumers.\n\nCallers name it: `letI := li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization_qEqOne`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.bar_holds_at_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.bar_holds_at_classical","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L104-L104","doc":"At q = 1, the identity holds for all n via the verified\nclassical-limit chain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.bar_holds_at","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.bar_holds_at","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The (q, n) pairs where the bar-symmetrization identity\nis established. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization","kind":"class","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L85-L104","doc":"The bar-symmetrization conjecture as a Lean class.\n\nFor each n ≥ 1 and each q ∈ R, the bar-symmetrized Faddeev\ncoefficient equals the symmetric Li_2^q coefficient.\n\nClass fields:\n- `bar_holds_at`: predicate naming the (q, n) pairs where\n  the identity is verified.\n- `bar_holds_at_classical`: discharges all n at q = 1 (the\n  classical-limit case, verified via li2qCoeff_at_q_eq_one).\n\nDownstream theorems consume the class via [Instance] per\nAGENTS.md §3b-cond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.li2qCoeff_bar_invariant_at_q_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.li2qCoeff_bar_invariant_at_q_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L78-L83","doc":"Bar invariance at q = 1: li2qCoeff 1 n = li2qCoeff 1⁻¹ n.\n**Verified** unconditionally via 1⁻¹ = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.li2qCoeff_at_q_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.li2qCoeff_at_q_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L70-L76","doc":"At q = 1, the symmetric Li_2^q coefficient reduces to the\nclassical 1/n². **Verified** unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qInteger_at_q_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qInteger_at_q_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L64-L68","doc":"At q = 1, [n]_1 = n. **Verified** unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.li2qCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.li2qCoeff","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The n-th coefficient of the symmetric Li_2^q series:\n[Li_2^q]_n = 1 / (n · [n]_q) for n ≥ 1; 0 at n = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qInteger_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qInteger_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L43-L56","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical classical-extended bracket.**  This site carries\n*two* guards, `n = 0` and `q = 1`, but only the second is doing work: at `n = 0`\nthe canonical `qIntBalCl` already returns `0` on both branches (`(0 : ℝ)` at\n`q = 1`, and `qIntBal q 0 = 0` otherwise).  So the extra `n = 0` case is\nredundant and the agreement is unconditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qInteger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qInteger","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Li2qPhiqBarSymmetrization.lean#L30-L41","doc":"The symmetric q-integer [n]_q = (q^n - q^{-n})/(q - q^{-1})\nas a real-valued function.\n- n = 0: returns 0\n- q = 1: returns n (classical limit)\n- otherwise: symmetric q-integer formula.\n\nStated over ℝ; the same definition transports to any field\nwhere (q - q⁻¹) is invertible. ","signatureChunk":0}]}